    pass 3 phase 2: review follow-ups — one row per deal in the window, staggered off-the-hour schedules, NULL-safe guards, no OK run without a slice
    
    Two critics (BigQuery platform, semantic parity) read commit bf473ba; every confirmed finding is folded in.
    
    sql/deals_landed_v1.sql: the table function's window keeps one row per deal (QUALIFY … ORDER BY fetched_at DESC) — a doubled slice
    (a delete-older that failed after its INSERT, a paged search repeating a deal) would abort the MERGE or insert the deal twice; the
    [window_start, run_ts) bound applies only when a window start is given, so an event keeps a deal created in run_ts's own second.
    sql/new_deals_batch.sql: guards NULL-safe (NOT IN / IF treat NULL as false); RAISE when the caller named raw_landing_failed and no
    slice exists (an OK run with 0 rows would otherwise advance C's watermark); rows_written = the MERGE's @@row_count; the horizon
    heuristic reads the window the rule reads (full when its oldest deal is ≥ 83 days old); the handler's ROLLBACK is wrapped so an
    engine-cancelled transaction cannot hide the FAILED row; duration_ms documented as ending at the transaction's opening.
    sql/scheduled_query.sh + .env.example: per-entity schedules off the hour (SEALSQ 03:53 UTC, ICALPS 04:23) — two scripts in one
    minute are cancelled as conflicting transactions and an on-the-hour schedule can trigger twice; the script refuses a shared minute
    or an on-the-hour value. Docs updated wherever 04:00 appeared.
    tests/test_pass3_sql.py (9 tests): the UDF's 12 arguments pinned positionally against scoring/hot_score_v1.sql; every element of
    every gaps literal checked; the new guards pinned; the vectors call passes CAST(NULL AS TIMESTAMP); generation behind --write.
    docs/PASS3_RAW_ROOT.md: both follow-up lists, the by-design divergences (rounding ties, SAFE_CAST vs _num, name_key '' vs NULL,
    twin order, deleted deals in the root), the 11-argument CALL in "Callers".
    
    Recipe: .claude/skills/aider-scaffold/assets/recipes/c_raw_batch.md
    Scaffolded-by: hand (no LLM key)
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
